<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Battle of Tarain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1191">1191</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Battle of Tarain was fought in 1191 near Taraori in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the Ghurid army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. The Rajputs won, and Muhammad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghor">Ghor</a> was wounded and carried from the field. He returned the following year and won the second battle on the same ground.</p></div>
